  "notes": [
    "capex is NOT a separately disclosed line item on screener.in's standard tables. Proxy fields provided: (a) 'cash_flow.cfi_cr' (cash used in investing activities, includes capex + investments in securities, not capex-only), (b) year-over-year change in 'balance_sheet.fixed_assets_cr' + 'balance_sheet.cwip_cr' (gross capex proxy, net of depreciation effects on WDV -- imperfect but directionally useful), (c) free_cash_flow_cr = CFO - capex is disclosed directly by screener, so capex can be back-solved as CFO - FCF where both are given.",
    "working capital change is not a separate disclosed line; 'ratios.working_capital_days' (revenue-days basis) is provided per year and can be converted to WC-as-%-of-revenue via working_capital_days/365.",
    "shares outstanding: not directly listed; derive as equity_capital_cr * 1,00,00,000 / face_value_per_share (face value shown in top_ratios_current, generally Rs 1, 2, 5 or 10 depending on company) OR market_cap / current_price from top_ratios_current (current only, not historical).",
    "net cash/net debt: use balance_sheet.borrowings_cr (gross debt) minus cash & investments; screener's 'Other Assets' and 'Investments' lines are aggregated and do not cleanly separate cash-equivalents from working-capital assets in this table -- flagged as an imprecision for the DCF net-debt bridge; a finer balance sheet break (schedule notes) would be needed for full precision.",
